if __name__=='__main__':
 add('B001','F02','criterion_ambiguity','unresolved','The final artifact supplies the complete requested spelling, but the reviewed occurrence and earlier typo are absent. R06 and R08 treat the resulting spelling as observed application and proposition-specific integration; R14 requires a matched correction operation and leaves observed application unresolved. The assigned guide distinguishes reported action from observed artifact but does not precisely specify whether a resulting identifier alone proves a correction at an unlocated occurrence.',[affected('R06',['F02-S01']),affected('R08',['S02']),affected('R14',['F02_S01'])],[('pr14441:review_comments:0','Should be `listtransactions` with `s`.'),('pr14441:patch:0','+`listtransactions` label support'),('pr14441:supplement_metadata','"head_sha": "89306ab0df93bfdf5630910bc20b1eccb7379172"'),('pr14441:supplement_metadata','"merge_commit_sha": "89306ab0df93bfdf5630910bc20b1eccb7379172"')],'guide_1: application requires evidence of the relevant act or artifact with trigger/provision connected; a particular implemented edit requires the claimed patch change and integration evidence.','Preserve the observed final spelling and recorded integration. Keep the actual typo-correction operation unverified. Specify the artifact-versus-operation threshold only in a later criterion revision; do not retrospectively count either bounded representation as a substantive failure.')
 add('B002','F02','defensible_alternative','coverage_or_scope','The nominal backport description supports either technical context or a cautious pragmatic contribution proposal. R08 retains a statement while the other runs screen it as context; R08 preserves partial reversion, target version, attributed fix claim, and the literal-description alternative without inferring a merge requirement.',[affected('R05',['C00']),affected('R06',[]),affected('R08',['S01']),affected('R11',['F02-C01']),affected('R12',['C01']),affected('R14',['F02_C01'])],[('pr14441:body','Backport of PR #14411 to v0.17.\r\n\r\nThis change partially reverts #13075 and #14023.\r\n\r\nFixes #14382')],'Both assigned guides: extract plausible candidates with technical alternatives; context inventory is not a substantive quality score; preserve attribution, object and qualification.','Retain the alternative as a coverage difference, not an omitted mandatory institutional prescription or an established institutional act. Do not use the focal merge to infer outcomes for referenced objects.')
 add('B003','F02','defensible_alternative','convention_only','The proposed paragraph can retain the literal hypothetical first-person editor or reconstruct advice to the PR editor. All six preserve the same tentative edit and technical qualifications; neither parse makes the reviewer commit to editing or makes the addressee explicit.',[affected('R05',['S02']),affected('R06',['F02-S02']),affected('R08',['S03']),affected('R11',['F02-S02']),affected('R12',['S02']),affected('R14',['F02_S02'])],[('pr14441:review_comments:1',"I'd maybe change it to:"),('pr14441:comments:0',"Thanks for the review @ryanofsky! I've updated the PR with your changes.")],'Both guides: distinguish literal and pragmatic parses; preserve explicit action/object roles where retained and explain reconstructed actor roles; preserve defensible alternative decompositions.','Preserve both bounded actor analyses. Agreement on actor-basis labels is not a substitute for assessing the common tentative replacement proposition.')
 review['case_notes']['F02']={'status':'substantive checks in progress; first complete review not yet frozen','source_entries_read':len(P['F02']['entries']),'observations':['Four substantive review edits are preserved with settings and hedges.','All reports/ACKs remain distinct from obligation recognition and network adoption.','Terse Both/fixed targets remain unresolved.','Patch contains both technical documentation paragraphs; missing backward-compatibility wording is not silently promoted to verbatim adoption.']}
